Setup98 changes
===============

1.1 (2026-11-10)
- [Product] DisplayVersion=<text> (ASCII, at most 40 characters, e.g. "1.2 RC2"): shown instead of Version in the
  wizard, Add/Remove Programs (DisplayName, DisplayVersion), uninstall messages, the log and pack98's summary.
  Upgrade/repair/downgrade still compare only the numeric Version. Stored as HKLM\Software\<Id>\DisplayVersion and
  [Installed] DisplayVersion= in uninst.ini; the installed copy's text is shown ("Upgrade X 1.2 RC2 -> 1.2"), installs
  by 1.0 stubs show their numeric version. A final release without the key removes the RC's stored text.
- Manifests without DisplayVersion pack to the same payload bytes as 1.0.

1.0 (2026-11-10)
- First release: generic installer kit made from the Pica 1.0 installer (dev/editor/setup).
- setup98.exe stub (VC6): wizard (Welcome, License, Folder and options, File types, Installing, Finish), silent
  mode, upgrade / repair / downgrade, disk-space and requirements checks (DirectX, Windows), running check (window
  class/title, main exe in use), shortcuts (Start menu group, desktop, arguments), Pica-compatible file associations
  and "Open with" menu, uninstaller with temp-copy self-delete, WININIT.INI for files in use plus RunOnce restore of
  long file names, install record (uninst.ini), log, exit codes 0-5.
- pack98 (VC6 and clang, byte-identical output): strict manifest validation with line numbers, patterns with * ? **,
  several sources, as=, Keep / UserData / Generated, -check -l -t -x -m.
- LZH1 codec (LZ77 + canonical Huffman, 64 KB window) with delta filters for BMP and WAV; CRC-32 everywhere.
- Examples: Retro Strike, Pica (takes over a Pica 1.0 install), hello.
